{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmXmDR8QzfYcUkHKxugn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both rows changed meaning (`VERDICT: MEANING rows=2`), and I re-anchored both. The verdict is committed as `7c736fe1` with the `WI: WI-835` trailer, in `docs/reviews/wi-835-coordinator-retained-adjudication/003-ADJUDICATE-6ca0b05.md`.\n\n- **SR-227 – MEANING, approved.** Compared with the 2026-10-05 anchor, retention now covers adjudications the coordinator starts as well as the loop's, both routes build one shared request, and a launch is refused if the dedicated home isn't signed in. An implementation that only covers the loop would fail the new text.\n  - The clause I returned last time is gone: the lane-worktree-only and in-deadline-verdict conditions now live in a new row, SR-231, which is still Drafted. Every remaining acceptance condition checks something the Requirement actually states.\n  - The acceptance cell no longer lists which inputs trigger a drain. That list now lives in LLR-270, the right tier for it.\n- **LLR-270 – MEANING, approved.** Before, the drain check used only the template of the brief being launched. Now it covers the template of every brief class the session is retained for.\n  - Two behaviours change: switching between retained brief classes no longer drains the session, and editing another retained class's template now does.\n  - The two tests named in the verdict file cover this, and it is the right reading of SR-227's \"the inputs it judges under change\".\n\nThe re-anchor act is committed as `dd55ccca`: `intake.py snapshot --reattests SR-227,LLR-270 --verdict <verdict file>`, recorded as act 38. The snapshot copies whole registries, so among the approved rows only SR-227 and LLR-270 changed. The new drafts SR-231, LLR-305 and LLR-306 were copied in still marked Drafted; nobody has approved them yet. I didn't change any registry cell.\n\nThe two follow-ups I drafted in earlier rounds have been answered within this lane (commit `6ca0b05c`), so intake will mint nothing for them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":758,"cache_read_input_tokens":126012,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":758},"output_tokens":696,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce1fccc0-8fec-4295-889e-541a0dc6f24a","uuid":"ff4fa557-b379-4832-bcf4-cc468b005227","timestamp":"2026-10-06T19:25:06.268Z","request_id":"req_011CfmXmD9Ff6yKJUBzAdE8W"}
